NAME
    testlab - create and operate live development scenario instances

SYNOPSIS
    testlab
    testlab scenarios
    testlab prepare scenario [scenario-arg ...]
    testlab status [instance-id]
    testlab context instance-id [key]
    testlab enter instance-id
    testlab close instance-id

DESCRIPTION
    testlab is the m developer-facing live scenario environment command.

    It prepares concrete development realities and keeps their lifecycle state
    persistent so an operator can leave an instance alive, inspect it, re-enter
    it later, or recover cleanup after a failed/interrupted preparation.

    testlab is not a test runner and does not produce PASS/FAIL assertions or
    formal validation evidence.

PROJECT SCENARIOS
    The physical current working directory at invocation is the project root.

    Scenarios are regular executable, non-symlink files under:

        testlab/scenarios/<scenario>

    Scenario names use the m controlled-name grammar. The scenario is invoked
    as a child program and is never sourced into testlab.

    Lifecycle phases are:

        check
        prepare
        enter
        cleanup

    check runs before persistent instance allocation and validates prerequisites
    without runtime mutation.

    prepare creates or binds resources, records ownership as resources are
    acquired, publishes factual context and returns after readiness.

    enter attaches the operator directly using the inherited terminal and
    standard streams.

    cleanup may destroy only resources recorded as owned and must support
    recovery after failed or interrupted preparation.

SCENARIO ENVIRONMENT
    check receives:

        TESTLAB_PROJECT_ROOT
        TESTLAB_SCENARIO_NAME

    prepare, enter and cleanup additionally receive:

        TESTLAB_INSTANCE_ID
        TESTLAB_INSTANCE_DIR
        TESTLAB_CONTEXT_DIR
        TESTLAB_RESOURCES_DIR

    Scenario arguments after the scenario name are passed to check and prepare.
    Later phases use persisted instance state.

    TESTLAB_CONTEXT_DIR contains factual handles for activities.

    TESTLAB_RESOURCES_DIR is the scenario's persistent ownership/recovery
    inventory. The first baseline defines no generic resource-record format.

INSTANCE STATE
    Persistent technical state is rooted by:

        state-path user sys testlab data

    Instance records live below its instances/ directory.

    Each instance contains a frozen executable copy of its selected scenario.
    enter and close use the frozen copy even if the project source later changes.

    States are:

        preparing
        ready
        failed
        closed

    failed and interrupted preparing instances remain available for diagnosis
    and close/recovery. Repeating close on a closed instance succeeds without
    running cleanup again.

    Closed records are retained; the baseline defines no automatic purge policy.

COMMANDS
    testlab
        Open the interactive-first menu. Project scenarios appear as new
        choices and persisted non-closed instances can be re-entered or closed.

    testlab scenarios
        Print discoverable scenario names in ascending bytewise lexical order.

    testlab prepare scenario [scenario-arg ...]
        Run check, allocate persistent state, freeze the scenario and run
        prepare. On success print the opaque instance id.

        A prepare failure after allocation leaves a failed persistent instance;
        the diagnostic includes its id for inspection and cleanup.

    testlab status
        List persisted instance id, scenario name and lifecycle state.

    testlab status instance-id
        Print id, scenario, state and project root, plus recorded failure data.

    testlab context instance-id
        List controlled context keys in ascending bytewise lexical order.

    testlab context instance-id key
        Write the selected context file verbatim.

    testlab enter instance-id
        Invoke the frozen enter phase of a ready instance.

    testlab close instance-id
        Invoke frozen cleanup for ready, failed or preparing instances, then
        mark the instance closed only after successful cleanup.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Success.
    1   Invalid invocation.
    2   Scenario, instance or context not found, or incompatible lifecycle state.
    3   Scenario lifecycle phase failed.
    4   testlab infrastructure or persistent-state failure.

    Signal-derived statuses from an interrupted interactive scenario may be
    propagated.

FILES
    bin/sys/testlab
        Public m command.

    res/sys/manual/testlab
        This operational manual topic.

    <project-root>/testlab/scenarios/
        Project-local scenario definitions.

    $(state-path user sys testlab data)/instances/
        Persistent scenario instance records.

EXAMPLES
    List scenarios:

        testlab scenarios

    Prepare, inspect, enter and close scratch:

        instance=$(testlab prepare scratch)
        testlab context "$instance"
        testlab context "$instance" root
        testlab enter "$instance"
        testlab close "$instance"

